# .gitignore for thu-net-autologin
#
# Design rule: ignore things by their EXACT run-time names, never by a loose glob that could also
# match a file the repository legitimately needs to track.  A pattern like "*user.txt" would have
# been the obvious shortcut and is exactly the kind of rule that silently swallows a real file
# later; every pattern below names a concrete artifact this tool actually creates.

# ---- credentials ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Custody of these belongs to the user's own %LOCALAPPDATA%, never to a checkout.  They are
# ignored by exact name in case someone points -CredentialDir at the repository directory itself.
ThuNet-user.txt
ThuNet-pass.dpapi
portal-user.txt
portal-pass.dpapi

# Any DPAPI blob, whatever it was named.
*.dpapi

# Generic backstops for hand-made copies.  These are patterns the repository has no file matching,
# so they cannot bite a tracked file.
*credential*.txt
*secret*.txt

# ---- machine-local state -------------------------------------------------------
# The learned ac_id is specific to the wall port this machine is plugged into and is re-learned
# automatically, so it must never be shared through the repository.
ThuNet-ac_id.txt
ac_id.txt
portal-acid.txt

# ---- logs and capture dumps ----------------------------------------------------
*.log
thunet-probe-capture.txt
thunet-login*.txt
thunet-probe*.txt

# ---- runtime directories -------------------------------------------------------
# Relative and therefore anchored at the repository root; this deliberately does NOT ignore a
# "docs/logs/" style directory elsewhere in the tree.
creds/
logs/
state/

# ---- editor and OS noise -------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
